# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# One line per program: <name> <class> <first-task>
#   class: user        runs on rv32emu (console output and exit code only)
#          mmio-in     needs device input (UART RX), so it is only built
#          vga         needs the VGA framebuffer (T5)
#          privileged  needs traps, CSRs other than the counters, or CLINT
# The benchmarks under benchmarks/ are listed here too, as VER-07 runs them.
# scripts/check-rv32emu.sh rejects a malformed or duplicate line and a program
# directory without one.
#
# jit runs from T1 on purpose: it is the directed fence.i program of T1-06.
# In T1 to T3 a store is visible to fetch at once, so fence.i only has to
# decode as a no-op for the stored instructions to run. From T4 on (T4-07),
# the same program checks that fence.i makes them visible to fetch.
#
# add, lw and beq are the directed programs of the observation bundles
# (OBS-03): main is in assembly, so a bundle shows the instruction it names.
# hazards holds the sequences of T4-02 (HazardSpec), for the pipeline view
# (OBS-09); it is a T4 program, though every core runs it.
add        user     T1
lw         user     T1
beq        user     T1
fibonacci  user     T1
quicksort  user     T1
sb         user     T1
strings    user     T1
muldiv     user     T1
jit        user     T1
qrcode     user     T1
uart       mmio-in  T1
dhrystone  user     T1
duremark   user     T1
ecall      privileged T3
irqtrap    privileged T3
hazards    user     T4
perf       privileged T3
vgatest    vga      T5
nyancat    vga      T5
qrcode-vga vga      T5
shell      mmio-in  T5
# The quiz programs: your routines in assembly, checked and costed on every task.
quiz-arith user     T1
quiz-sine  user     T1
quiz-nn    user     T1
quiz-enc   user     T1
